{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779760746,"nonce":"yms2g27TH3idEt88GhrR8XT2I+I=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDow9yg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/165#issuecomment-4539039178"},"message":"**Closing — root cause identified; implementation tracked in [`rolker/unh_marine_navigation#33`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/33) (with the recovered legacy code as the port reference).**\n\n**Root cause: momentum overshoot at the survey-leg → hover transition — *not* battery, *not* environmental set.**\n\nCross-event analysis of all genuine hover engagements (gated on `current_nav_task ∈ {done_hover, hover_override}`, ≥15 s, departure-filtered — full method/figures under #169 §13):\n\n- **12/12 hovers drift off the point** — median **9.2 m** (up to ~13 m), still moving outward at 15 s, settling ~20–40 s. The hover holds the **position at the instant of engagement** → post-engagement *overshoot*, not the \"pre-convergence approach\" the title implied.\n- **Battery (candidate #1) rejected** — no SOC correlation (22.2–24.7 V uniform); station-keeping is far from any low-SOC thrust-authority limit.\n- **Environmental set rejected** — velocity-at-engagement is **12/12 coast** (decays from ~1.5 m/s; drift aligns with pre-hover velocity); drift bearing matches the **survey-leg heading**, not the logged forcing (current westward→slack, wind light south). Carried momentum.\n\n**Mechanism:** `marine_nav_behaviors::Hover` is a position-only proportional controller — no velocity/decel term — so it can't anticipate the stop. The `deceleration_` param is declared but unused: the fossil of a pre-nav2 stop-point projection deferred in the nav2 port.\n\n**Fix (in [unh_marine_navigation#33](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/33)):** restore the stop-point projection — the legacy `predict_stopping_pose.cpp` + `HoverTask` wiring are **intact in git history** (`1c5db5a^`) and are the port reference — plus an optional live `point_at_target` param (ArduPilot `LOIT_TYPE` analog). Validated against ArduPilot Rover Loiter (the earlier \"more efficient than hover\" observation). Shared/cross-platform code → on-water re-validation required.","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1779760747,"nonce":"4HBS+udKbRnMdlNphv2p9TpLu/s=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ0DM88AAAAGCoubcA"},"status":2}]}